sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as preC-SUMO Adapter
    participant P as preCICE

    Note over S,P: Initialize
    S->>P: precice::Participant(...)
    S->>P: setMeshVertices(csumo_2d_nodes)
    S->>P: setMeshVertices(csumo_3d_nodes)
    S->>P: setMeshVertices(sources_sinks_nodes)
    S->>P: requiresInitialData()
    alt Initial outgoing data required
        S->>S: Report configuration error and return -1
        Note over S,P: No initial response is written
    else No initial outgoing data required
        S->>P: initialize()

    loop While isCouplingOngoing() returns true
        S->>P: isCouplingOngoing()
        S->>P: dt = getMaxTimeStepSize()
        Note over S,P: dt is the full preCICE time window with no internal timestep or subcycling
        S->>P: readData(csumo_2d_nodes, relative time = dt)
        S->>P: readData(csumo_3d_nodes, relative time = dt)
        Note over S,P: First iteration uses initialized FM fields at t = 0
        Note over S,P: Later iterations use FM fields received by the previous advance()
        S->>S: convertNFtoConnectedSinkSources(settings, NF2FF responses, received FM 3D fields)
        Note over S: Create connected source/sink dataset using the FM fields just read
        Note over S: Excess constituents become absolute using received FM intake constituents
        S->>P: isTimeWindowComplete()
        alt preCICE reports a completed window
            S->>P: resetMesh(sources_sinks_nodes)
            S->>P: setMeshVertices(sources_sinks_nodes, updated vertices)
        else Window not complete
            Note over S: Retain the registered source/sink mesh
        end
        S->>P: writeData(source/sink geometry, discharge, momentum, C01-C10)
        Note over S,P: Dataset uses previously exchanged FM fields, not FM fields arriving in this advance()
        S->>P: advance(dt)
        Note over S,P: Data exchange and remeshing synchronization
    end
    S->>P: isCouplingOngoing() returns false

    Note over S,P: Cleanup
    Note over S: Return from run() with automatic cleanup
    Note over S,P: No explicit finalize() call in the current loop
    end
